# Git Workflow Guidelines

## Mục tiêu

Tài liệu này định nghĩa các nguyên tắc và best practices cho việc sử dụng Git trong Cursor Enterprise Framework. Mục tiêu là đảm bảo consistent codebase, clear history, efficient collaboration, và safe deployments thông qua disciplined Git practices.

Git là fundamental tool cho modern software development. Việc tuân thủ consistent Git workflow giúp teams collaborate effectively và maintain healthy codebase.

## Nguyên tắc cơ bản

### 1. Branching Strategy

Understanding GitFlow và trunk-based development.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    GitFlow Strategy                               │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                  │
│  Main Branch:                                                    │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  main ────────────────────────────────────────────────────│
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                              │                                    │
│  Release Branches:                                                │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  release/1.0 ──────────────────────────────────────────│  │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                              │                                    │
│  Development:                                                   │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  develop ───────────────────────────────────────────────│  │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│         │           │           │                               │
│  Feature Branches:                                            │
│  ┌──────▼──┐ ┌──────▼──┐ ┌──────▼──┐                         │
│  │ feature │ │ feature │ │ feature │                          │
│  │   /A   │ │   /B   │ │   /C   │                           │
│  └─────────┘ └─────────┘ └─────────┘                            │
│                                                                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 2. Branch Naming Conventions

Consistent branch names.

```bash
# Branch naming patterns
# Pattern: <type>/<ticket-id>-<short-description>

# Feature branches
feature/PROJ-123-add-user-authentication
feature/PROJ-456-implement-order-history
feature/PROJ-789-fix-payment-bug

# Bugfix branches
bugfix/PROJ-101-fix-login-error
bugfix/PROJ-102-correct-calculation-bug

# Hotfix branches
hotfix/PROJ-200-security-patch
hotfix/PROJ-201-critical-bug-fix

# Release branches
release/v1.0.0
release/v1.1.0

# Changelog convention
# feat: new feature
# fix: bug fix
# docs: documentation
# style: formatting
# refactor: code refactoring
# test: adding tests
# chore: maintenance
```

### 3. Commit Messages

Clear và descriptive commits.

```bash
# Good commit message format
# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>

# Examples
feat(auth): add JWT token refresh functionality

Implement token refresh mechanism to extend user sessions
without requiring re-authentication. This includes:
- New /auth/refresh endpoint
- Token rotation logic
- Redis-based token blacklist

Closes PROJ-123
Ref: #456

# Commit types
feat:     - New feature
fix:      - Bug fix
docs:     - Documentation
style:    - Formatting, missing semicolons, etc.
refactor: - Code refactoring
perf:     - Performance improvement
test:     - Adding tests
chore:    - Maintenance tasks
revert:   - Revert commit
```

```bash
# Angular commit convention
# Commitizen format
git commit

# Interactive selection
? Select the type of change that you're committing:
  feat:     - A new feature
  fix:      - A bug fix
  docs:     - Documentation only changes
  style:    - Changes that do not affect the meaning of the code
  refactor: - A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
  perf:     - A code change that improves performance
  test:     - Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
  chore:    - Changes to the build process or auxiliary tools

# Subject line (72 chars max)
# Imperative mood: "add" not "added" or "adds"

# Body (wrap at 72 chars)
# Explain WHAT and WHY, not HOW
```

### 4. Pull Request Workflow

Structured PR process.

```markdown
<!-- PR Template -->
## Description
<!-- What does this PR do? -->

## Type of Change
<!-- Mark all that apply -->
- [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change)
- [ ] New feature (non-breaking change)
- [ ] Breaking change
- [ ] Documentation update

## Testing
<!-- How was this tested? -->
- [ ] Unit tests added/updated
- [ ] Integration tests added/updated
- [ ] Manual testing performed

## Screenshots (if applicable)
<!-- Add screenshots for UI changes -->

## Checklist
- [ ] Code follows project style guidelines
- [ ] Self-reviewed
- [ ] Comments added for complex logic
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] No console errors or warnings
- [ ] Dependent issues linked

## Related Issues
<!-- Link to issues -->
Closes #123
Related to #456

## Additional Notes
<!-- Any additional context -->
```

```bash
# PR workflow commands
# Create feature branch
git checkout -b feature/PROJ-123-user-auth

# Make changes
git add .
git commit -m "feat(auth): implement user login"

# Push and create PR
git push -u origin feature/PROJ-123-user-auth

# After review feedback
git add .
git commit -m "fix(auth): address PR feedback"
git push

# Squash and merge
git checkout main
git pull
git merge --squash feature/PROJ-123-user-auth
git commit -m "feat(auth): implement user login"
git push
```

### 5. Merging Strategies

Safe merging practices.

```bash
# Merge strategy for feature branches
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git merge --no-ff feature/PROJ-123-user-auth

# No fast-forward to preserve branch history
# --no-ff creates a merge commit even for fast-forward

# Rebase before merge (cleaner history)
git checkout feature/PROJ-123-user-auth
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/develop

# Resolve conflicts
# Edit conflicting files
git add .
git rebase --continue

# After rebase, force push
git push --force-with-lease

# Hotfix workflow
git checkout main
git pull
git checkout -b hotfix/PROJ-200-security
# Make changes
git commit -m "fix(security): patch vulnerability"
git checkout main
git merge --no-ff hotfix/PROJ-200-security
git tag v1.0.1
git push origin main --tags
git push origin hotfix/PROJ-200-security  # For merge to develop
```

### 6. Git Hooks

Automated quality checks.

```yaml
# .huskyrc
{
  "hooks": {
    "pre-commit": "npm run lint && npm run type-check",
    "commit-msg": "commitlint -E HUSKY_GIT_PARAMS",
    "pre-push": "npm run test",
    "pre-rebase": "npm run test"
  }
}
```

```bash
# commitlint.config.js
module.exports = {
  extends: ['@commitlint/config-conventional'],
  rules: {
    'type-enum': [
      2,
      'always',
      ['feat', 'fix', 'docs', 'style', 'refactor', 'test', 'chore']
    ],
    'subject-case': [2, 'never', ['sentence-case', 'start-case', 'pascal-case', 'upper-case']]
  }
};
```

```bash
# pre-commit hook - lint-staged
# package.json
{
  "lint-staged": {
    "*.ts": ["eslint --fix", "prettier --write"],
    "*.{json,md}": ["prettier --write"]
  }
}
```

