## Anti Patterns

### 1. Large Commits

```bash
# Không nên - monolithic commit
git commit -m "Implemented everything"

# Nên - small, focused commits
git commit -m "feat(auth): add login endpoint"
git commit -m "feat(auth): add registration endpoint"
git commit -m "fix(auth): resolve password validation"
```

### 2. Force Pushing to Main

```bash
# Không nên
git push --force origin main

# Nên - never force push to protected branches
# If needed, create revert commit
git revert <commit-sha>
git push origin main
```

### 3. Committing to Wrong Branch

```bash
# Không nên - working on main
git commit -m "feature work"  # On main!

# Nên - always work on feature branches
git checkout -b feature/PROJ-123
git commit -m "feat: implement feature"
# Cherry-pick or rebase to fix
```

### 4. Ignoring Conflicts

```bash
# Không nên - force push to overwrite
git push --force

# Nên - resolve conflicts properly
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/main
# Edit conflicting files
git add .
git rebase --continue
```

### 5. No Code Review

```bash
# Không nên - self-approve
git commit -m "fix: my bug fix"
git push origin main  # No review!

# Nên - require reviews
# Configure branch protection rules
# Require PR approvals
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Atomic Commits

```bash
# Each commit should represent one logical change
# Good: "add validation for email field"
# Bad: "add validation and fix styling and update tests"
```

### 2. Branch Protection

```bash
# GitHub branch protection
# Settings > Branches > Add rule

# Require:
# ✓ Require pull request reviews before merging
# ✓ Require status checks to pass before merging
# ✓ Require branches to be up to date before merging
# ✓ Require linear history
# ✓ Include administrators
# ✓ Do not allow bypassing the above settings
```

### 3. Conventional Commits

```bash
# Standard format
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

# Types
feat:     New feature
fix:      Bug fix
docs:     Documentation
style:    Formatting
refactor: Refactoring
test:     Tests
chore:    Maintenance

# Breaking changes
feat!: Breaking change
fix!: Breaking change

# With scope
feat(auth): Add OAuth support
fix(payment): Correct currency calculation
```

## Workflow

### 1. Feature Development

1. Create branch from develop
2. Write code and commit frequently
3. Keep branch updated with develop
4. Open PR when ready
5. Address review feedback
6. Squash and merge

### 2. Hotfix Process

1. Create branch from main
2. Implement fix
3. Test thoroughly
4. Get expedited review
5. Merge to main and tag
6. Merge to develop

### 3. Release Process

1. Create release branch from develop
2. Perform release testing
3. Fix any issues
4. Merge to main
5. Tag release
6. Merge back to develop

## Ví dụ

### Ví dụ 1: Complete Feature Workflow

```bash
# Start feature
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b feature/PROJ-123-user-authentication

# Work on feature
git add src/auth/
git commit -m "feat(auth): add authentication module structure"

git add src/auth/login/
git commit -m "feat(auth): implement login endpoint"

git add src/auth/register/
git commit -m "feat(auth): implement registration endpoint"

# Update with latest develop
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/develop

# Push feature branch
git push -u origin feature/PROJ-123-user-authentication

# Create PR via GitHub/GitLab
# Address review comments
git add .
git commit -m "fix(auth): address PR feedback"
git push

# After approval, squash and merge
# Via GitHub UI or CLI
```

### Ví dụ 2: Hotfix Workflow

```bash
# Critical bug in production
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git checkout -b hotfix/PROJ-200-critical-bug

# Implement fix
git add src/
git commit -m "fix: resolve critical data race condition"

# Test locally
npm run test
npm run test:integration

# Push and create PR
git push -u origin hotfix/PROJ-200-critical-bug

# After review, merge to main
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git merge --no-ff hotfix/PROJ-200-critical-bug

# Tag the release
git tag -a v1.0.1 -m "Hotfix: resolve critical bug PROJ-200"
git push origin main --tags

# Merge to develop
git checkout develop
git merge --no-ff hotfix/PROJ-200-critical-bug
git push origin develop

# Clean up
git branch -d hotfix/PROJ-200-critical-bug
```

### Ví dụ 3: Release Workflow

```bash
# Prepare release
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b release/v1.1.0

# Update version
npm version minor --no-git-tag-version
git add package.json
git commit -m "chore: bump version to 1.1.0"

# Run release tests
npm run test
npm run test:integration
npm run test:e2e

# If issues found
git commit -m "fix(release): resolve test failures"
git push

# Merge to main
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git merge --no-ff release/v1.1.0

# Tag release
git tag -a v1.1.0 -m "Release version 1.1.0"
git push origin main --tags

# Merge back to develop
git checkout develop
git merge --no-ff release/v1.1.0
git push origin develop

# Clean up
git branch -d release/v1.1.0
```

